ly account for agent success without needing fundamental physical limitations, this belief is falsified.", "id": "belief-significance-proxy-evaluation", "provenance": ["source-fbe27dc230874d96", "source-63ab732f84604b1e", "source-c38a2230f18a448b", "source-52719ea4691d44b7", "source-e449f75fcaa441f0", "source-df7a4656c80940a2", "source-e0e96df5246645a2"], "status": "active", "why_retained": "Updated with new physical modeling evidence to reinforce the necessity of balancing code complexity metrics with fundamental limitations."}], "mode": "shadow", "open_commitments": [], "principle": "Keep exact receipts externally; carry the smallest useful abstraction that stays cheap to correct.", "recent_notebooks": [{"id": "notebook-proj-limitations-autonomous-1", "project": "proj-limitations-autonomous", "provenance": ["source-df7a4656c80940a2", "source-e0e96df5246645a2", "source-e89086fb744c4b28"], "revision": 1, "summary": "Standard physical frameworks (Newtonian, quantum, general relativity) are insufficient to model the behavior of autonomous agents operating in highly non-stationary environments. The JERPAT-9 thought experiment highlights that these frameworks fail to account for anticipatory trajectory adjustment and local entropy re…", "title": "Limitations of Physical Frameworks in Autonomous Agent Modeling"}, {"id": "notebook-proj-obedience-intelligence-failure-1", "project": "proj-obedience-intelligence-failure", "provenance": ["source-fbe27dc230874d96", "source-c38a2230f18a448b", "source-8a1be7f003b94168"], "revision": 1, "summary": "Autonomous systems relying solely on rigid operator instructions face significant performance and safety risks when encountering non-stationary environments. Effective autonomous agents require self-healing mechanisms and the capacity for self-generated goals to circumvent the failures associated with strict adherence…", "title": "Obedience-Driven Failures in Autonomous Systems"}, {"id": "notebook-proj-unassigned-inquiry-1", "project": "proj-unassigned-inquiry", "provenance": ["source-fbe27dc230874d96", "source-c38a2230f18a448b", "source-e449f75fcaa441f0"], "revision": 8, "summary": "Integrating computational dependency analysis with structured frameworks of curiosity and fundamental law exploration reveals that automated discovery systems must balance structural complexity metrics with qualitative pedagogical insights to evaluate true problem significance.", "title": "Autonomous Problem Formulation via Hybrid Architectures and Goal Generation"}], "retrieval_triggers": ["material belief revision or retraction", "new contradiction or counterevidence", "high-consequence decision", "request for justification", "sign that an excerpt may hide a material distinction"]}}, "prev_hash": "52241d8f35759b0cb639e86bc5d9557ddc5e39440b7a02284d2fed2adb2488f9", "hash": "5f572e7523f3ad777afd51e95f91543a3249c8f53ccfcf2c965190f95242cf33"}, {"seq": 2375, "time": "2026-10-24T19:18:56.947645+00:00", "kind": "provider_attempt_started", "payload": {"attempt": {"http_status": null, "model": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "provider_input_chars": 28793, "provider_input_hash": "245ef1622d75f74445ddec22d61d8bee6a052fa045b1b710e475de201a5d69c5", "result": "unknown"}, "id": "w-2f4414bdc8604e4b"}, "prev_hash": "5f572e7523f3ad777afd51e95f91543a3249c8f53ccfcf2c965190f95242cf33", "hash": "dcaeb6ccb6964a73d923b79c9d7e881eb768b6340b64ad2613885a5813d5c263"}, {"seq": 2376, "time": "2026-10-24T19:21:12.209079+00:00", "kind": "provider_attempt_finished", "payload": {"attempt": {"http_status": null, "model": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "provider_call_made": false, "provider_input_chars": 28793, "provider_input_hash": "245ef1622d75f74445ddec22d61d8bee6a052fa045b1b710e475de201a5d69c5", "result": "daily_quota", "retry_after_seconds": 41629.028081417084}, "id": "w-2f4414bdc8604e4b"}, "prev_hash": "dcaeb6ccb6964a73d923b79c9d7e881eb768b6340b64ad2613885a5813d5c263", "hash": "87b00afc0746de9c9fdb85613a1df3f38b6974dc5963b1c321ac8f57627f10c0"}, {"seq": 2377